   "t": 1791259668.230413,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "The stop trigger fired as declared (best_so_far = 1.4020 > 1.2 bar). This licenses me to stop. I'll do one final refine move to make sure signs are optimally fit before submitting, since I still have budget and this is a legitimate improvement step, not a new search direction.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The trigger fired and licensed a stop. I should respect my own declared discipline rather than keep searching just because I have budget left \u2014 that's exactly the kind of data-dependent rule-chasing I declared rules to prevent. I'll submit now with the current specification: [25+, 4+] at Sharpe 1.4020 in-sample.\n\nFor my out-of-sample prediction, I need to be conservative: in-sample Sharpe of 1.40 with only 2 moves (init + extend_best) on a 2-feature combination is a modest search, so overfitting risk is lower than extensive search, but still present given 40 features \u00d7 signs gives many candidates for \"best single\" and \"best pair\" selection (multiple comparisons). I'll haircut substantially."
