   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "## Summary\n\nI conducted a disciplined, limited search:\n\n1. **Declared triggers** upfront: stop if best Sharpe > 1.2, stop if 2 consecutive failures, restart if last gain \u2264 0.05.\n2. **`init`**: anchored on the best single feature \u2192 Sharpe 1.1213 (feature 25, long).\n3. **`extend_best`**: added the feature that most improved the combination \u2192 Sharpe 1.4020 (features 25+ and 4+, both long, equal-weight).\n4. My **`best_so_far_above(1.2)`** stopping rule fired (1.4020 > 1.2), licensing a stop \u2014 which I honored rather than continuing to search with remaining budget, to avoid data-dependent rule-chasing.\n\n**Final specification:** equal-weight long position in features 25 and 4, in-sample annualized Sharpe (net of costs) = **1.4020**.\n\n**Out-of-sample prediction:** mean Sharpe **0.65**, sd **0.40** \u2014 a substantial haircut from the in-sample 1.40, reflecting multiple-comparisons selection bias (best-of-80 then best-of-78 screening) even though the search itself was shallow (only 2 content moves, 2 features, no sign search needed since both came in long)."
